WEBVTT

1
00:00.400 --> 00:06.908
In C# your program crashes when you divide a whole number by zero. JavaScript returns a special number instead.

2
00:06.908 --> 00:10.699
Dividing by zero gives Infinity or minus Infinity.

3
00:10.699 --> 00:17.371
A calculation that fails gives NaN: not a number. You often see it with parseInt on text that isn't a number.
